## The greatest Int.
##
## # Parameters
## - `v`: a DynArray.
##
## # Returns
## `Some` of it, or `None`.
##
## # Examples
## ```pyking
## use mutation
## import dynarray
## v = dynarray([3, 1, 2])
## print(dynarray.maximum(v))
## ```
## ```stdout
## Some(3)
## ```
public def int::maximum(v: DynArray(Int)) -> Option(Int):
    list.maximum(list(v))


